            <div xml:id="d165">

                <pb facs="0263" n="255" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg255"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/2144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-06-06T22:00:00+09:00">June 6, 1941—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 6—noon.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>783. Embassy’s 774, June 6, 1 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The associate mentioned in second sentence of telegram under reference
                        called on me this afternoon and definitely corroborated the information
                        conveyed in paragraph numbered 1 of aforesaid telegram.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>In the light of the foregoing information and our general observation of
                        the political situation in Tokyo, I am now inclined to question the accuracy
                        of the alleged message from the Prime Minister reported in Embassy’s 765,
                        June 4, 10 p.m. Much political maneuvering is going on in Japan at the
                        present time.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
